LibreDWG 0.14.8597: fix false "buffer underflow" past 256 MiB on LLP64 (Windows)

bit_advance_position() (src/bits.c:74) tests for a negative result with

    else if ((long)(pos + advance) < 0)

pos is a size_t bit position (dat->byte * 8 + dat->bit). On Windows x64
(LLP64) long is 32 bits, so the cast truncates the 64-bit bit position:
once the byte offset in the decompressed buffer reaches 2^28 (256 MiB,
i.e. bit position 2^31) the truncated value is negative, the "buffer
underflow" branch fires and the chain is reset to byte 0. Every following
bit read (bit_read_B/BB/3B/RC all call bit_advance_position) then decodes
garbage from the start of the buffer. On LP64 (Linux, macOS) long is
64 bits, so the bug does not show there.

Fix: detect underflow by comparing magnitudes instead of casting to long.
On LP64 the condition is equivalent to the old one for all reachable
positions, so Linux/macOS behaviour is unchanged.

--- a/src/bits.c
+++ b/src/bits.c
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@
                  ", advance by %ld",
                  __FUNCTION__, dat->byte, dat->bit, dat->size, advance);
     }
-  else if ((long)(pos + advance) < 0)
+  else if (advance < 0 && pos < -(size_t)advance)
     {
       loglevel = dat->opts & DWG_OPTS_LOGLEVEL;
       LOG_ERROR ("buffer underflow at pos %" PRIuSIZE ".%u, size %" PRIuSIZE

LibreDWG 0.14.8597: dwg2dxf skips blocks after a block holding a POLYLINE or an INSERT with attributes
(added 2026-10-18)

dxf_block_write() (src/out_dxf.c) passes the caller's loop index `i` - the BLOCK_HEADER index of
dxf_blocks_write() - to dwg_dxf_object() for the BLOCK record and every owned entity. For a POLYLINE
(and an INSERT with ATTRIBs) dwg_dxf_object() advances that index past the object's VERTEX/SEQEND
(ATTRIB/SEQEND) objects, which is right for the object-array walk of the ENTITIES section but here
moves the BLOCK_HEADER loop forward, so the next BLOCK_HEADERs are never written: their INSERTs then
reference blocks that have no definition in the DXF, silently (no ERROR). Seen on real AutoCAD 2007-2018
drawings (bound xrefs, room tags, equipment blocks, _ArchTick): 62 blocks over 11 drawings, 0 with
this fix. The fix gives dwg_dxf_object() a local index inside dxf_block_write().

--- a/src/out_dxf.c
+++ b/src/out_dxf.c
@@ -3894,7 +3894,8 @@
 
   if (obj && obj->fixedtype == DWG_TYPE_BLOCK)
     {
-      error |= dwg_dxf_object (dat, obj, i);
+      int j = (int)obj->index; // see below: never the caller's loop index
+      error |= dwg_dxf_object (dat, obj, &j);
     }
   else
     {
@@ -3987,7 +3988,15 @@
                              != mspace_ref
                       && obj->tio.entity->ownerhandle->absolute_ref
                              != pspace_ref)))
-            error |= dwg_dxf_object (dat, obj, i);
+            {
+              // A local index: dwg_dxf_object advances it past the VERTEX/SEQEND
+              // or ATTRIB/SEQEND objects of a POLYLINE or INSERT, which is right
+              // for the object-array walk in dxf_entities_write but here would
+              // move the caller's BLOCK_HEADER loop index (dxf_blocks_write) and
+              // skip the following blocks without any error.
+              int j = (int)obj->index;
+              error |= dwg_dxf_object (dat, obj, &j);
+            }
           obj = get_next_owned_block_entity (hdr, obj); // until last_entity
         }
     }
